#import "@local/mindtape:0.2.0": *

#show: task.with(
  title: "speconaut cannot read a MindTape config that MindTape itself writes",
  tags: ("speconaut", "mindtape", "interop", "upstream"),
  priority: 8,
  difficulty: 3,
  status: done(2026, 8, 2),
)

== Summary

\`speconaut check truth/\` fails with \`.mindtape/config.toml: parse error: unknown field \\\`on\\\`, expected one of \\\`project\\\`, \\\`tasks\\\`, \\\`ls\\\`, \\\`rm\\\`, \\\`templates\\\`, \\\`add\\\`, \\\`go\\\`, \\\`typst\\\`\`.

The config it rejects was generated by \`mt init --preset gated\`, and \`mt check\` accepts it — 55 tasks valid. So the two tools disagree about the schema of a file one of them authored.

The cause is version skew. speconaut takes a path dependency on \`../mindtape/crates/mindtape\` for its task model and config validation, but the installed binary (speconaut 0.1.0, from the nix profile) was built against a mindtape predating the \`\[\[on.flip\]\]\` hook block. Installed \`mt\` is 0.2.0 and emits it.

This is a dependency bug and belongs upstream, not worked around in paogen. But it blocks the whole truth tree from validating, so the hooks are commented out in \`.mindtape/config.toml\` with a pointer to this task. That is a recorded interim, not a fix.

What is lost meanwhile: the \`into("wip")\` hook that lists what is already in flight, and — more importantly — the \`into("done")\` gate that refuses to close a task still carrying the template's TODO placeholders. The gated preset's whole argument is that a status is a stamp rather than proof, and that gate is the only part of it a machine enforces.

== Acceptance criteria

- \`speconaut check truth/\` parses \`.mindtape/config.toml\` without error, with the \`\[\[on.flip\]\]\` blocks restored and uncommented.
- speconaut builds against the current mindtape checkout at all. It does not today: \`cargo build\` fails with \`failed to read /home/tank/projects/home/mindtape/crates/swhid-mint/Cargo.toml — No such file or directory\`. mindtape restructured its crates and speconaut's \`Cargo.toml\` still names the old paths, so "rebuild it against current mindtape" is not currently an available move. That is the first thing to fix and it may be the whole fix.
- The fix is in speconaut, not in paogen's config. If the schema genuinely diverged rather than lagged, the divergence is reconciled upstream and recorded there.
- The skew is known to span at least two keys, so it is a version gap rather than one missed field. \`on\` surfaces first; commenting it out reveals \`tasks.comments\` behind it. Do not chase them one at a time — commenting out enough of the preset to satisfy the old parser means deleting the strictness the preset exists for.
- \`mt check\` still passes on the same file, so the two tools agree.
- The \`into("done")\` gate demonstrably refuses a task still containing \`TODO:\`.
- A note in speconaut records how the two crates stay in step, since a path dependency plus a separately-installed binary will drift again otherwise.

== Non-goals

- Changing paogen's MindTape preset or relaxing the gated rules to fit an older parser. The config is correct; the reader is behind.
- Pinning paogen to a locally-built speconaut binary. The agent guide explicitly warns against reaching for an in-tree build as a fallback, because it drifts the other way.
- Rewriting the hooks to avoid \`\[\[on.flip\]\]\`.

== Files

- \`~/projects/home/speconaut/\` (the actual fix)
- \`.mindtape/config.toml\` (restoring the commented hooks once the fix lands)

== Result

No file changed here, because the fix had already landed upstream and nobody had
checked. speconaut's Cargo workspace was repointed at the extracted sibling
crates on 2026-07-31 — \`swhid-mint\` now resolves at \`../swhid-mint\` rather than
the \`../mindtape/crates/swhid-mint\` path this task recorded as missing — so
speconaut could rebuild against current mindtape again, and the installed binary
stopped lagging. The hooks in \`.mindtape/config.toml\` are uncommented and have
been for some time.

The point of this entry is that "it passes now" was not accepted as proof. A
check that silently skips the file it is meant to read passes exactly as
convincingly as one that reads it, so the parse was made to fail on purpose
before it was believed. Against a scratch copy of \`.mindtape/\`, \`.speconaut/\`
and \`truth/\`:

#table(
  columns: 3,
  [*Config under test*], [*Result*], [*What it proves*],

  [The tree's own config, hooks uncommented],
  [\`All specs valid (4 features)\`, exit 0],
  [Nothing on its own. This is the reading the task would have accepted.],

  [Plus an extra \`\[\[on.flip\]\]\` block on \`into("blocked")\`],
  [\`All specs valid (4 features)\`, exit 0],
  [The key whose rejection opened this task is understood, not merely tolerated — a second, previously unseen instance of it parses too.],

  [Plus an unknown key under \`\[tasks\]\`],
  [\`check failed: 2 error(s)\`, exit 1],
  [The file is genuinely parsed and validated. A skipped file cannot produce this.],
)

\`tasks.comments\` — the second key the task warned was hiding behind \`on\` — is
present in the live config that parses clean, so the version gap closed as a gap
rather than one field at a time. \`mt check\` agrees on the same file: 107 tasks
valid. And the gate the preset exists for was made to fire rather than assumed:
a throwaway task carrying \`- TODO: \` placeholders was refused at
\`mt done\` with exit 1 and the configured message, so the \`into("done")\` hook
is live, not decorative.

One criterion is deliberately left unmet: the note recording how speconaut's
embedded mindtape and the separately-installed \`mt\` stay in step. That is a
design call belonging to speconaut, the mechanism is not paogen's to choose, and
speconaut's tree currently carries uncommitted changes that are not this
session's. Filed rather than written badly from the outside. The defect this
task names is fixed; the guard against its recurrence is not, and saying so is
more useful than a note that invents a mechanism nobody agreed to.

That guard lived here as \`speconaut-mindtape-skew-guard\` until 2026-08-03,
naming no paogen file at all. The owner ruled that a task fixing another
project belongs in that project's tracker, so it moved to speconaut's own
backlog as \`keep-the-embedded-mindtape-in-step-with-the-installed-mt\` and
was retired here. paogen is still what breaks when the two drift; it is simply
not where the fix can be written.
